# .vscode/ is deliberately TRACKED. It used to be ignored (as *.vscode*),
# so the editor config was local-only: when VS Code lost the cached
# interpreter the settings could not restore it, and Pylance fell back to a
# system python with no homeassistant installed, which surfaced as ~80 bogus
# "could not be resolved" import errors.
# Personal overrides that should stay local:
.vscode/*.local.json
.github/**/*instruction*
*samples*
# pyrightconfig.json is tracked on purpose: without an explicit pythonVersion
# Pylance falls back to an older interpreter and reports bogus errors against
# this codebase. Only the per-machine override stays ignored. This replaces an
# earlier "*pyrightconfig*" pattern, which silently excluded the tracked file.
pyrightconfig.local.json
*quality_scale.yaml*
log.txt
*diag-sample.json*
*log.log*
*pycache*
*.mypy_cache*
*.pytest_cache*
*.ruff_cache*
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
junit.xml
.venv
*venv*
